======================================================================================================================
SUMMARY
======================================================================================================================
  Does the dark fluid's conversion run away through the web?  Partly -- yes through the collapsed and turned-around web at
  z <~ 1.5, no through the voids, and not at z >~ 3.
  Nominal cell: the smooth (non-halo) carrier converts f_web = 0.03/0.21/0.60/0.76 at z = 3/2/1/0 (most conservative bracket
  0.01/0.07/0.29/0.56); with the halos, F_tot = 0.36/0.55/0.81/0.91 (halo only
  0.34/0.43/0.53/0.63).  The converted web is one connected set.
  What drives it: the halos' own daughters seed the multistream and turned-around web around them (momentum matching through
  the infall), and turned-around sheets ignite by themselves on the zero-strain cone.  What stops it: expanding flow (no
  re-resonance; the voids keep 92% of their carrier), and the gate at high z (rho_t/rho_bar = 36/68 at z = 3/4).
  Across the band: F_tot(0) 0.74-0.90, F_tot(1) 0.58-0.75; S8 ratio 0.931 (nominal).

  checks: 12/13 pass; load-bearing failures: 1   [518s]
exit code: 1
